        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ഭരണം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഭരണം — bharaṇaṁ — \"administration; rule\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പുതിയ ഭരണം ജനങ്ങൾക്ക് ഇഷ്ടമായി. putiya bharaṇaṁ janaṅṅaḷkkŭ iṣṭamāyi. The people liked the new administration."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Under a rule: -ന്റെ ഭരണത്തിൽ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഭരണം (bharaṇaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit bharaṇa, \"bearing, maintaining\" (CDIAL 9395; Monier-Williams), from the root bhṛ, \"to bear\": to rule is to bear the load of a land."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
